ased sometime in season  two and while there was some community  criticism for the last bundle just being  a skin put on the operator daniel in a  survey corpse outfit this roland  operator looks like an actual titan  but in other shooter news a change.org  petition demanding that players be  allowed to refund battlefield 2042 now  has over  120 000 signatures the petition which  started on february 2nd calls ea's  release of the latest battlefield title  a quote mockery of every customer who  purchased this video game with the goal  of showing just how many people want  full refunds the petition's creator  satoshi nakamoto suggested a  class-action lawsuit could be filed  although it's unclear whether such a  case would have any chance of succeeding  at the time of this recording ea has  provided no indication that it plans to  offer refunds nor is there any sign of  this petition having an effect outside  of standardized systems such as steam's  refund policy publishers offering  refunds on games is an extremely  uncommon practice with one notable  recent exception being cyberpunk 2077.  many fans of the battlefield franchise  have been disappointed by battlefield  2042 and since its launch this past  november the game has been plagued by  numerous bugs which have kept developer  dice busy sorting them out however the  team has been so busy squashing the  game's bugs that it hasn't been able to  focus on extra content for the game  recently dice delayed the game's first  season which was supposed to add a new  map and specialist to this summer so be  honest with me did you sign that  petition  now be extra honest with me did you sign  that petition knowing you don't have a  copy of the game you just saw a report  and wanted to be a part of it or be a  troll  let me know in the comments  [Music]  you
 

